create a new source file called sprcol-demo.c
add makefile entriews to compile it to sprcol-demo.prg and to run it 
use vera-utils.h
it should set up vera so that sprites are active and sprite collision interrupts are enabled
create two sprites 
sprite 1 is an 32x32 white square with the bottom right quarter transparent, at position (100, 100)
sprite 2 is an 32x32 red square with the top left quarter transparent, at position (150, 150)
both sprites have collision mask 1001
set up an interrupt handler for sprite collision 
the interrupt handler will print the message "interrupt handled" and set a global bool variable collision to true
in the main loop, each time any key is pressed, move sprite 1 by (1,1) and check if collision is true
if collision is true, print the sprite collision bits from VERA.irq_flags